---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
---
<Base title="How HeyDock Works | Understand, Scope, Deliver, Support" description="HeyDock engagements follow a simple path: understand the brief, write a scope, deliver the agreed work, and leave a way to raise the next issue." canonicalPath="/how-we-work" keywords="how HeyDock works, IT engagement process, IT project approach">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">How we work</p>
    <h1>Understand, scope, deliver, support</h1>
    <p class="lede">A short path that stays the same whether the work is a single visit or a longer programme.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section white"><div class="wrap prose">
    <h2>Understand</h2>
    <p>We start with the people, the site or systems, and the constraint you do not want discovered later: access, a brand rule, a change window, a piece of kit we must not touch. A short, specific brief is more useful than a long, vague one.</p>
    <h2>Scope</h2>
    <p>You receive a written picture of what is in, what is out, and what 'done' looks like. If we cannot do the work, we will say so and, where we can, point to a better front door. A visit is not booked until city, skills and access are confirmed.</p>
    <h2>Deliver</h2>
    <p>We work to the agreed scope. If the job grows, we stop and ask. Changes that can drop a service go in a window. White-label rules, if they exist, are followed on site and in writing.</p>
    <h2>Support</h2>
    <p>Handover includes a way to raise the next issue. Ongoing support is a written arrangement, not an implied retainer. Documents and policies, including <a href="/support-and-escalation">support and escalation</a> and <a href="/vendor-onboarding">vendor onboarding</a> for MSP partners, sit alongside this page.</p>
  </div></section>
  <CtaBand />
</Base>
